{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/962459-how-much-does-benediction-cost-in-2e","id":962459,"title":"How much does Benediction cost in 2e?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-02T13:14:29-07:00","id":962459,"title":"How much does Benediction cost in 2e?","content":"I just noticed that the Mortal Remains update doesn't really mention how much Benedictions would cost in the new xp system. It was 5 xp in the old system, without a scaling cost (since there were no dot ratings to benedictions) and this doesn't have a clear conversion path to 2e. Specialties are the only other thing that had a flat cost (3 xp). Specialties only cost 1 xp now, if I doubled that, it would be 2 xp. That's my best conversion effort.<br /> <br /> But other people's views would be helpful.<br /> <br /> Also, one of the things I've loved about 2e is that it no longer incentivizes the min/maxing of 1e. (Where it was just always smarter to start with your attributes, merits, skills or power stat high because of the scaling xp costs).<br /> <br /> The fact that you get free benedictions at character creation based on your dots in the benediction merit seems like another example of this that has unfortunately been carried over because the stopgap conversion of mortal remains. Anyone have any ways around it that don't feel like totally robbing players of free xp? Otherwise it's just silly to not start character creation at 5 in Benediction.<br /> <br /> This probably also applies to Castigations and whatever other endowments behave this way that I'm unaware of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6422-lionel","name":"Lionel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-02T14:49:13-07:00","id":962512,"title":"","content":"The official response was:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/125154-mortal-remains-not-quite-as-much-a-change-to-endwoments-as-i-hoped?p=125176#post125176\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/125154-mortal-remains-not-quite-as-much-a-change-to-endwoments-as-i-hoped?p=125176#post125176\"> Mortal Remains - not quite as much a change to endwoments as I hoped - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/125154-mortal-remains-not-quite-as-much-a-change-to-endwoments-as-i-hoped?p=125176#post125176\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/125154-mortal-remains-not-quite-as-much-a-change-to-endwoments-as-i-hoped?p=125176#post125176 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I had been quite looking forward to Mortal Remains since I heard about it, after all, Hunter is a very flexible line with lots of thematic and fun groups, both among the compacts and the conspiracies. For me, there has always been one rather nasty side of the line and that was balance and structure. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum